{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["plan"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Update a draft"},"description":"Use this when the user wants to change a draft post, or schedule it: \"shorten the caption\", \"move it to\n        Friday 6pm\", \"turn comments on\", \"set the YouTube title\", \"add a first comment\", \"put it in my playlist\", \"use\n        my usual preset\", \"schedule it\". post_id: from get_post_stats with status \"draft\". schedule=true schedules it\n        (YouTube Shorts and TikTok): only after the user saw this exact post and said yes, and only with the publish\n        permission. Set only what was asked: caption, scheduled_at (ISO 8601 with its offset) or clear_time,\n        platform, account_id (list_social_accounts), privacy (TikTok public, followers, friends, private; YouTube\n        public, unlisted, private). TikTok, off until the user says: allow_comment, allow_duet, allow_stitch,\n        disclose (then brand_organic or brand_content), aigc, mode direct or inbox. YouTube: title, category (a\n        name), playlist_id (list_youtube_playlists) or new_playlist, made_for_kids (needed to schedule), tags,\n        notify_subscribers, synthetic. first_comment: Instagram, Facebook (also title). Instagram: share_to_feed,\n        collaborators, audio_name. reply_control: Threads, Bluesky (also alt). post_preset: a name from\n        list_post_presets. clear: title, category, playlist, tags, first_comment, collaborators, audio_name or alt.\n        The answer lists what platforms would still refuse.\n        Not for: scheduled or posted posts (refused), new drafts (draft_post, plan_posts), covers (set_post_cover) or\n        removing a draft (delete_draft). Free. Without schedule=true it stays a draft.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"account_id":{"default":"","title":"Account Id","type":"string"},"aigc":{"anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"null